ATTRIBUTION & EDUCATIONAL PURPOSE NOTICE
================================================================================

MiniVec is an independent educational software project developed from scratch 
for the study and practice of AI engineering, vector indexing concepts, and 
high-performance Python system architecture.

During the preliminary research phase (Phase 2 - Project Design), architectural 
concepts and vector search paradigms were studied with reference to the 
open-source vector search engine Qdrant (https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant).

Important Disclaimers:
1. MiniVec is NOT a fork, copy, or drop-in replacement for Qdrant.
2. None of Qdrant's Rust source code or proprietary implementation details 
   are copied or included in this project.
3. MiniVec is designed specifically for pedagogical and learning purposes, 
   focusing on first-principles understanding of vector representations, 
   distance metrics, filtering, persistence, and evaluation in Python.
4. "Qdrant" is a trademark of Qdrant Solutions GmbH. This project is not 
   affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Qdrant Solutions GmbH.
